===Etymology===
{{der|de|goh|stanga}}, from {{der|de|gem}} ''*stangjo-''. Compare English ''[[stang]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈʃtaŋə/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Stange.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aŋə|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|Stange|Stangen}}

# [[pole]]; [[bar]]; [[rod]]; [[post]] {{gloss|a long stick, usually round and of metal, but also of other material, especially when fixed somewhere}}
# a small straight [[glass]] for beer, especially [[Kölsch]]
# {{lb|de|of cigarettes}} [[carton]] {{gloss|lengthy box containing several packets}}
# {{lb|de|chiefly in {{m|de|eine Stange Geld}}}} a lot (of money); a [[packet]]
# {{lb|de|in {{m|de|von der Stange}} or compounds}} {{l|en|run-of-the-mill}}, chiefly with clothes (referring to the poles on which clothes are presented in large fashion shops)
#: '''''Stangen'''kleidung ist mir nicht individuell genug.''
#:: I find '''run-of-the-mill''' garments lacking in individuality.

